{"seconds": 51.5, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! The main line is:\n1. **c6** (pawn push setting up an unstoppable promotion threat)\n   - Black's best try is **Nxb1** (capturing the hanging rook)\n2. **c7** \n   - Black gives check with **Nd2+**\n3. **Kg2**\n   - Black's best is **Rxb5** (trying to stop the b-pawn)\n4. **c8=Q#** \u2013 Checkmate!\n\nThe motif is a **promotion** (the pawn reaching the 8th rank with checkmate), but more fundamentally this is about advancing passed pawns that are unstoppable. The key insight is that Black cannot stop both the c and b pawns.\n\n**Coaching note (80 words max):**\n\n\"When you have two advanced passed pawns, they're often worth more than active pieces. After Nc3 attacks your rook, play c6! Even if Black takes your rook, c7 advances unstoppably. Black can't defend both pawns: if they capture on b5, c8=Q is checkmate. The lesson: with widely separated passed pawns deep in enemy territory, a rook is expendable. Push the pawns.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"c6\", \"line\": [\"c6\", \"Nxb1\", \"c7\", \"Nd2+\", \"Kg2\", \"Rxb5\", \"c8=Q#\"], \"motifs\": [\"promotion\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38", "square": "c6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38", "square": "b6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38", "square": "b1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1r5k/6pp/5p2/1PP5/5P2/2n3P1/5P1P/1R3K2 w - - 2 38", "move": "c6"}}, {"tool": 